+# Implementation Plan: Task identifiers
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+## Technical Context
+Language TypeScript on Node (type stripping), Dependencies none, Storage in-memory (N/A), Testing `node --test` via `npm test`, Project Type library.
+
+## Constitution Check
+- No new dependency: pass. No clock/randomness: ids come from a per-list counter (`t1`, `t2`, …). 
+- Domain never throws: `get` returns Result. TSDoc on exported functions; public API via `src/index.ts` (Task type already exported). Tests in `test/list.test.ts`.
+
+## Design
+- `Task` gains `readonly id: string`. `createTask(input, id)` takes the id.
+- `list.ts`: a counter in the closure; tasks stay keyed by title in the map; a private `resolve(ref)` first looks for a task whose id equals the trimmed ref, then falls back to the title. `find` and `change`/`remove` use it. `get(id)` matches ids only.
+- Existing test with `deepEqual` on a task is updated to include the id.
